WEBVTT

00:12.053 --> 00:14.389
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:15.223 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.852 --> 00:22.230
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:22.313 --> 00:26.484
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:26.568 --> 00:29.195
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.279 --> 00:32.449
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:32.532 --> 00:34.951
♪ You'll be free ♪

00:35.035 --> 00:38.371
♪ From all the things you used to be ♪

00:40.040 --> 00:42.042
[birds chirping]

00:50.759 --> 00:55.305
DOONA!

01:01.936 --> 01:03.146
[Won-jun sighs]

01:03.897 --> 01:04.814
[exhales]

01:05.899 --> 01:07.025
[exhales]

01:11.738 --> 01:12.572
[grunts softly]

01:14.908 --> 01:16.910
[gentle music playing]

01:19.329 --> 01:20.580
[Doona] Would you allow it?

01:22.332 --> 01:25.001
[Won-jun chuckles]
What kind of question is that?

01:25.710 --> 01:27.420
If you want to perform, you should.

01:28.046 --> 01:29.798
I'd love to see you sing, you know?

01:32.008 --> 01:33.760
I would support you no matter what.

01:34.761 --> 01:36.930
I forget sometimes how naive you are.

01:42.894 --> 01:44.854
What if they say we can't be together?

01:45.688 --> 01:46.773
Then what?

01:46.856 --> 01:48.650
[dramatic music playing]

01:48.733 --> 01:50.819
[In-wook] Given what's at stake,
no one's dumb enough

01:50.902 --> 01:52.862
to add a boyfriend to the equation.
You got it?

01:52.946 --> 01:55.281
Not the label, not even Doona.

01:58.159 --> 01:59.661
So who should leave who alone?

02:00.453 --> 02:01.496
Take a guess.

02:01.579 --> 02:03.581
[inaudible]

02:22.433 --> 02:23.518
[cheering and applause]

02:24.185 --> 02:27.188
EPISODE 9
DOONA!

02:27.272 --> 02:28.231
[Doona] Thank you.

02:31.192 --> 02:32.694
CONGRATS ON THE COMEBACK!

02:32.777 --> 02:35.989
ALL OF MSA WISHES YOU SUCCESS
IN YOUR SOLO CAREER, DOONA!

02:38.283 --> 02:39.200
Ah!

02:40.910 --> 02:42.912
[emotional music playing]

02:44.038 --> 02:47.792
FROZEN WATER PIPE PREVENTION TIPS

02:55.008 --> 02:57.927
[Won-jun] I moved.
I'll give you my new address.

02:59.304 --> 03:00.263
THE CONSTITUTION

03:00.346 --> 03:01.389
It's colder now.

03:02.015 --> 03:03.183
I hope you're staying warm.

03:03.266 --> 03:05.226
2022 LEVEL 5 OPEN COMPETITIVE RECRUITMENT

03:07.687 --> 03:09.689
We don't have any photos together.

03:10.607 --> 03:12.150
Let's take some when we have time.

03:12.233 --> 03:13.693
2. EXAM SCHEDULE BY JOB CATEGORY

03:21.409 --> 03:23.411
[overlapping chatter]

03:24.996 --> 03:27.290
[man] I love you! Doona!

03:27.373 --> 03:28.666
[man 2] Look over here, please.

03:28.750 --> 03:30.126
[indistinct chatter]

03:32.170 --> 03:34.672
- [Doona] Hello.
- [girl] Hello. Here. I brought you a gift.

03:34.756 --> 03:37.217
- So sweet. Thank you.
- Yeah, oh my gosh. You're so pretty.

03:38.343 --> 03:40.178
These glasses are pretty cool.

03:40.261 --> 03:42.931
- You don't mind if I try them on, right?
- Um…

03:43.014 --> 03:45.058
[Doona] Where do they
even sell these things?

03:47.435 --> 03:49.979
Hey there, can you find out
where these are from real quick?

03:50.605 --> 03:52.607
Oh, and see this guy to the door.

03:54.192 --> 03:55.318
[man] Security, please.

03:57.320 --> 03:59.781
[indistinct chatter]

03:59.864 --> 04:01.115
[man 3] Yeah, you're a disgrace.

04:03.868 --> 04:06.996
IT'S SMOOTH ENOUGH
TO DOWN IN ONE!

04:08.915 --> 04:10.083
[chuckles softly]

04:13.044 --> 04:15.004
You seem pretty shy. What's your name?

04:16.256 --> 04:17.966
Doona, hello there. [chuckles nervously]

04:18.049 --> 04:21.928
♪ Screaming out so loud ♪

04:27.433 --> 04:28.977
Are you serious?

04:29.060 --> 04:31.062
[curious music playing]

04:33.606 --> 04:34.440
Is it…

04:35.233 --> 04:36.192
It couldn't be.

04:39.821 --> 04:41.864
TO SU-JIN FROM DOONA
GO, KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE!

04:41.948 --> 04:45.201
[cheering]

04:45.285 --> 04:46.536
Whoo!

04:46.619 --> 04:48.955
[laughing]

04:51.040 --> 04:53.626
MINSONG TOGETHER FESTIVAL
OUTDOOR CONCERT, LEE DOONA

04:53.710 --> 04:55.003
[Won-jun sighs]

04:55.086 --> 04:57.922
I'm so busy preparing
for the end of the semester.

04:58.840 --> 04:59.757
[sighs]

04:59.841 --> 05:01.843
[emotional music playing]

05:07.890 --> 05:09.475
I really miss you.

05:13.229 --> 05:15.231
- [pop music playing outside]
- [fans cheering]

05:26.409 --> 05:29.996
It feels like…
we're in two different worlds.

05:37.253 --> 05:39.672
[indistinct chatter]

05:42.175 --> 05:43.468
[girl] She is so pretty!

05:43.551 --> 05:45.553
[indistinct chatter]

05:52.894 --> 05:56.022
For us to have met
and to sit side by side

05:56.105 --> 05:57.899
feels purely by chance.

05:59.942 --> 06:02.195
[In-wook] Yes, we just finished,
and we're on the road.

06:03.196 --> 06:04.113
About an hour?

06:05.782 --> 06:07.408
The article's out the day after tomorrow.

06:07.492 --> 06:09.369
It's all been confirmed
with the team in Japan,

06:09.452 --> 06:11.079
so keep it under wraps until then.

06:16.084 --> 06:18.086
[somber music playing]

06:32.767 --> 06:33.768
[Won-jun sighs]

06:34.894 --> 06:37.105
[Won-jun] I feel angry today
for some reason.

06:47.949 --> 06:49.534
CRAM SCHOOL

06:51.828 --> 06:52.912
[Won-jun] It's snowing.

06:53.955 --> 06:55.998
The semester ends in a few days.

06:58.251 --> 07:00.420
And my tutoring job ends soon too.

07:03.214 --> 07:04.132
[grunts]

07:22.900 --> 07:23.943
[sighs]

07:31.409 --> 07:34.954
It's cold out, but I haven't
seen that street cat Nana around.

07:35.663 --> 07:37.582
I'll look for her again tonight.

07:46.716 --> 07:47.675
[sighs]

08:03.065 --> 08:05.067
[mysterious music playing]

08:21.792 --> 08:23.252
Are you finished for the day?

08:24.629 --> 08:26.005
Want something to eat?

08:38.518 --> 08:39.519
Cheers.

08:47.652 --> 08:49.278
So you must've called a lot.

08:50.029 --> 08:50.863
Not really, no.

08:53.241 --> 08:54.116
Oh, really?

08:55.701 --> 08:57.411
I was sure you were worried sick.

08:58.454 --> 08:59.664
Well, that's good, then.

09:07.713 --> 09:08.631
[sighs]

09:09.215 --> 09:11.842
They took my cell away,
so I couldn't message you at all.

09:12.510 --> 09:14.387
In fact, I barely snuck out tonight.

09:17.848 --> 09:21.227
Well, that's good, and…
you don't have to explain at all.

09:22.353 --> 09:25.356
I know you were…
born to be singing up on the stage.

09:29.193 --> 09:30.194
You'll do great.

09:38.286 --> 09:39.287
Is everything…

09:41.289 --> 09:42.748
okay with us, Won-jun?

09:46.794 --> 09:48.004
I have to serve soon.

09:53.968 --> 09:54.969
Oh yeah?

10:00.850 --> 10:01.809
Well, that's great.

10:02.310 --> 10:04.395
At least that will help time pass quickly.

10:07.565 --> 10:08.524
[Won-jun sighs]

10:15.489 --> 10:18.200
My agency treats me as if I'm crazy.
[chuckles]

10:18.993 --> 10:20.202
They won't let me near a phone,

10:20.286 --> 10:23.331
and I can't even go to the bathroom
without someone chaperoning me.

10:23.414 --> 10:24.999
They're scared I'll run away again.

10:25.750 --> 10:27.293
It's all so unnecessary.

10:30.046 --> 10:32.465
I guess I understand
why they're like this. Hmm.

10:54.945 --> 10:57.198
So, um, given the situation
with where we are,

10:57.698 --> 10:59.909
it'll be another two years max
I won't be here.

11:00.409 --> 11:02.036
Do you think you can handle that?

11:02.995 --> 11:06.374
Once I'm well established,
my private life won’t matter then.

11:07.625 --> 11:08.584
After that, we can date.

11:08.668 --> 11:10.044
[Won-jun] You don't need to, uh…

11:17.635 --> 11:18.928
Don't worry about me.

11:22.306 --> 11:24.350
[somber music playing]

11:27.311 --> 11:28.354
[Doona sighs]

11:35.027 --> 11:36.821
You wanna give up just like that?

11:37.321 --> 11:38.280
Seriously?

11:39.407 --> 11:40.700
Isn't that what you were saying?

11:42.326 --> 11:43.911
No, I wasn't saying that.

11:49.792 --> 11:51.043
Well, that's what I'm saying.

11:54.797 --> 11:56.757
I think I wanna break up with you.

12:27.872 --> 12:31.500
So when I was a washed-up has-been,
you never had a problem with us dating.

12:31.584 --> 12:33.961
Now, 'cause I'm a star, you can't take it?

12:34.044 --> 12:36.297
Seriously,
what difference does it make, Won-jun?

12:39.008 --> 12:41.343
When I met with him last night,
do you know what I said?

12:42.178 --> 12:43.637
I told him you and I were dating

12:44.513 --> 12:46.432
and we're not about to let it end!

12:47.308 --> 12:49.310
[Doona panting]

12:52.229 --> 12:53.939
Because I want you in my life.

12:55.524 --> 12:57.818
We've already gotten this far,
so why end it now?

13:00.905 --> 13:03.032
I don't understand what changed for you.

13:04.200 --> 13:06.494
So what's the point of me holding on?

13:08.078 --> 13:09.789
What could you have been going through

13:10.998 --> 13:12.166
compared to me?

13:13.000 --> 13:15.127
You were the one
who said I should go back.

13:16.420 --> 13:18.631
You said you wanted to see me sing.

13:32.186 --> 13:33.771
It's you who's letting go.

13:35.314 --> 13:37.525
You're the one
that's breaking your promise.

13:38.025 --> 13:40.903
You're running away from this
because you don't have the guts.

13:41.695 --> 13:43.572
You're leaving like all they all did.

13:46.200 --> 13:47.868
You're no different from the rest, okay?

13:51.580 --> 13:52.581
Am I right?

13:52.665 --> 13:54.667
[emotional music playing]

13:56.585 --> 13:57.586
[Doona] Am I right?

14:04.093 --> 14:05.177
Apparently.

14:51.140 --> 14:52.808
[alarm beeping]

14:52.892 --> 14:54.894
[train approaching]

15:29.053 --> 15:30.220
[sobbing]

16:17.059 --> 16:19.061
[crying]

16:50.551 --> 16:52.553
[airplane approaching]

16:54.722 --> 16:56.515
[pop music playing]

16:57.391 --> 16:59.101
[indistinct chatter]

17:05.357 --> 17:06.525
[woman] Yeah, that's good.

17:09.319 --> 17:10.154
[man] Action!

17:20.539 --> 17:22.541
[mysterious music playing]

17:48.525 --> 17:50.986
[pop music playing]

18:13.008 --> 18:13.842
I'VE MOVED

18:13.926 --> 18:14.760
I MISS YOU

18:14.843 --> 18:16.762
IT FEELS LIKE
WE'RE IN TWO DIFFERENT WORLDS

18:16.845 --> 18:19.807
FOR US TO HAVE MET AND TO SIDE BY SIDE
FEELS PURELY BY CHANCE

18:19.890 --> 18:22.017
[emotional music playing]

18:27.940 --> 18:29.358
[Yun-taek] So, what is dating?

18:29.942 --> 18:31.735
Dating is a muscle.

18:32.903 --> 18:34.238
Muscle!

18:36.990 --> 18:37.991
Uh…

18:39.451 --> 18:40.369
Muscle.

18:41.120 --> 18:42.538
Here's how to think of it.

18:42.621 --> 18:45.749
We've all been torn down
at some point in life, haven't we?

18:46.500 --> 18:49.294
Being torn down, as well as feeling pain,

18:49.378 --> 18:51.380
is necessary for building muscle.

18:51.463 --> 18:52.673
[students] Oh.

18:52.756 --> 18:54.591
In fact, that's how we get stronger.

18:54.675 --> 18:56.176
DATING = MUSCLE

18:56.260 --> 18:58.720
Yes, even your heart may bulk up.

18:59.763 --> 19:02.057
Bulking… uh…

19:03.058 --> 19:04.184
bulking up your heart.

19:04.268 --> 19:05.644
[students laugh]

19:05.727 --> 19:07.771
So, everyone, dating is what again?

19:07.855 --> 19:09.189
[students] It's a muscle.

19:09.273 --> 19:11.441
Louder. Tell me, what is dating again?

19:11.525 --> 19:13.026
[students] It's a muscle!

19:13.110 --> 19:15.028
- [Yun-taek] What is it?
- [students] It's a muscle!

19:15.112 --> 19:16.530
[Yun-taek] One last time.

19:16.613 --> 19:18.699
- [students] It's a muscle!
- [Yun-taek] It's a muscle!

19:18.782 --> 19:21.827
You can do it! Yes, we can all
have love in our lives again.

19:21.910 --> 19:24.371
Just bulk up your heart! Yeah!

19:24.454 --> 19:25.539
- Yeah!
- [students cheering]

19:25.622 --> 19:28.959
Let's all bulk up for… our love!

19:29.042 --> 19:30.294
[students] Seo Yun-taek!

19:52.107 --> 19:53.859
- [I-ra] Hey!
- [Won-jun grunts]

19:53.942 --> 19:55.402
[I-ra] Hey!

20:00.741 --> 20:03.869
Get up and eat breakfast.
I have to leave for work pretty soon.

20:10.125 --> 20:12.920
- Hurry up, huh?
- All right.

20:19.009 --> 20:19.968
[sighs]

20:33.232 --> 20:34.107
[sighs]

20:37.945 --> 20:39.154
[I-ra] I'm off to work.

20:41.156 --> 20:43.450
Ah, you're up early,
given how much you drank last night.

20:43.533 --> 20:45.953
- Yeah, I meant to go home and sleep.
- [I-ra] Hot, hot!

20:46.036 --> 20:48.622
I'll do that. You should grab
a protein bar or something.

20:53.377 --> 20:55.671
This one's for you. This one's for you.

20:57.130 --> 20:58.840
- And don't forget this!
- Thank you.

21:01.051 --> 21:02.844
- I'll get going!
- Have a good day.

21:02.928 --> 21:03.929
[I-ra chuckles]

21:04.721 --> 21:05.806
Okay, bye for now.

21:08.725 --> 21:10.686
Her job's going well, huh?

21:11.186 --> 21:14.231
Who would've thought…
that I-ra'd take a desk job.

21:14.314 --> 21:16.024
Or that I'd actually live with a girl!

21:16.608 --> 21:18.694
- Yeah, that's weird.
- [door beeps]

21:18.777 --> 21:20.779
I'm not sure I'll ever get used to that.

21:22.322 --> 21:23.991
I gotta head out.
Take your time, all right?

21:24.074 --> 21:25.075
Thanks.

21:30.414 --> 21:31.623
[door beeps, opens]

21:39.298 --> 21:40.340
[sighs]

21:40.424 --> 21:42.175
- [boy] Hey, wait for us.
- [girl] Won-jun!

21:43.343 --> 21:45.012
- [Won-jun] Hello.
- [girl] Hey.

21:48.890 --> 21:50.517
[pop music playing]

21:54.730 --> 21:56.857
HANG IN THERE!
MAYBE DREAM SWEET WILL VISIT?

21:56.940 --> 21:59.067
TO SU-JIN FROM DOONA
GO, KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE!

22:06.366 --> 22:07.492
[bell jingles]

22:08.076 --> 22:11.747
The people at the Oseong Apartment
are saying they asked for pickled ginger.

22:11.830 --> 22:13.498
- They want it now.
- Huh?

22:15.751 --> 22:18.795
It wasn't on their order.
What are they saying? [sighs]

22:19.338 --> 22:20.672
[dialing]

22:21.256 --> 22:22.758
[line ringing]

22:23.258 --> 22:25.635
Uh, hi. I'm calling you
from Su-jin's Seafood House.

22:25.719 --> 22:27.596
You just complained about an order here?

22:27.679 --> 22:30.724
Just so you know, if you want ginger,
you have to order it on its own.

22:35.228 --> 22:36.980
Okay, it'll be a bit longer.

22:38.315 --> 22:39.149
I'll take it.

22:39.232 --> 22:42.402
Won-jun, I think they're messing with us
'cause you look like a pushover.

22:42.486 --> 22:44.988
- I'll deal with this.
- No, I can handle it. Give it here.

22:45.072 --> 22:46.406
Hey, I said I'll go, okay?

22:47.115 --> 22:48.992
You should chill with Jin-ju.

22:49.076 --> 22:50.077
What?

22:50.702 --> 22:51.536
Over here.

22:54.206 --> 22:55.248
Oh.

22:55.791 --> 22:59.836
[chuckles] I was starting to wonder
if you were even going to notice.

22:59.920 --> 23:01.463
You didn't feel me glaring?

23:01.546 --> 23:03.799
So, uh, when did you get back?

23:03.882 --> 23:05.467
Um…

23:05.967 --> 23:07.886
[chuckles] You should sit down.

23:09.638 --> 23:12.891
This is the desert in Las Vegas.
Check these out.

23:12.974 --> 23:15.769
- What are those? Boulders?
- Exactly. Aren't they pretty?

23:15.852 --> 23:18.855
- Wow, that's really cool.
- [Jin-ju chuckles]

23:18.939 --> 23:20.607
- And here's Times Square.
- I recognize that.

23:20.690 --> 23:22.818
Wait, that's where they
drop the ball for the new year.

23:22.901 --> 23:26.113
- Right, that's exactly it.
- [Kooksu] I wish I could've gone.

23:26.196 --> 23:27.739
And here are my friends from Brazil.

23:28.365 --> 23:30.534
So this guy is an amazing photographer.

23:30.617 --> 23:31.868
He's seriously awesome.

23:31.952 --> 23:32.953
[Won-jun and Kooksu] Oh.

23:33.036 --> 23:35.580
- [Kooksu] He's a good-looking dude.
- [chuckles]

23:35.664 --> 23:37.416
[Jin-ju] They took this
on my way to school.

23:37.499 --> 23:39.835
And this is the restaurant
across from where I was staying.

23:39.918 --> 23:41.962
I'm there every day.
The food's seriously so good!

23:42.045 --> 23:44.756
- [Kooksu] It's called Habibi?
- It is. [chuckles]

23:45.257 --> 23:48.260
- The weather in Brazil is just amazing.
- [Kooksu] Ah. It looks awesome.

23:49.177 --> 23:52.305
- [Jin-ju] Oh, and look at this here.
- Wow. That looks amazing.

23:52.389 --> 23:54.599
Oh, I wanna go one day.

23:54.683 --> 23:57.102
- I'll start cleaning up. You keep talking.
- Okay.

23:57.769 --> 23:59.521
Ah, here's I-ra's parents' place.

23:59.604 --> 24:02.983
It was hard to find a place in Brazil,
so that's where I did a homestay.

24:03.692 --> 24:06.653
I originally went to visit.
Who knew I'd stay so long?

24:09.030 --> 24:09.906
Oops.

24:13.827 --> 24:15.454
- [Won-jun sighs]
- [Jin-ju] Um…

24:16.621 --> 24:19.624
Uh, Doona had a concert in Brazil,
so I went and saw her sing.

24:20.584 --> 24:21.418
Hmm.

24:23.962 --> 24:25.255
What are you doing tonight?

24:25.338 --> 24:28.049
Uh, my sister and I are hanging out.

24:28.133 --> 24:30.343
- She's picking me up later.
- Cool.

24:34.764 --> 24:35.682
Hmm.

24:43.523 --> 24:48.945
SU-JIN'S SEAFOOD HOUSE (DELIVERY-ONLY)

24:51.114 --> 24:52.032
[grunts softly]

24:54.034 --> 24:56.036
[humming]

25:11.009 --> 25:13.011
[somber music playing]

25:32.322 --> 25:35.158
CONGRATS ON THE 4-YEAR ANNIVERSARY
OF YOUR DEBUT AS A SOLO ARTIST!

25:43.375 --> 25:45.377
[alarm beeping]

25:48.004 --> 25:50.006
[train approaching]

26:03.061 --> 26:04.145
[train doors open]

26:16.491 --> 26:19.619
LOVE AND DO WHAT YOU WILL

26:21.079 --> 26:23.164
[somber music continues]

26:33.049 --> 26:35.510
So, is the house being demolished?
Have you heard anything?

26:36.344 --> 26:37.304
[Yun-taek] This house?

26:38.305 --> 26:41.516
I'm pretty sure that the landlord is gonna
remodel the whole thing for her son.

26:41.600 --> 26:43.893
He's getting married,
so it'll be a wedding gift.

26:44.644 --> 26:47.439
Ah, whoever that man is, I'm so jealous.

26:47.522 --> 26:51.568
Does that mean this is the last time
we'll all be here together like this?

26:51.651 --> 26:53.278
That's so depressing.

26:53.361 --> 26:54.529
[Yun-taek] Yeah, it is.

26:55.196 --> 26:57.490
Let's cheers.
It's been a while, everyone. Yep.

26:58.783 --> 27:00.368
Ah! Doona's missing here.

27:01.453 --> 27:05.040
It's not a full family reunion
if Doona isn't here to celebrate with us.

27:05.123 --> 27:06.583
Ah, Doona should've--

27:06.666 --> 27:09.586
You should eat more veggies
if you wanna stay healthy.

27:09.669 --> 27:11.671
How about we toast to everyone's health?

27:11.755 --> 27:13.590
- To everyone's health!
- To everyone's health!

27:13.673 --> 27:14.507
[Jin-ju] Cheers!

27:21.014 --> 27:23.975
- You aren't drinking much. How come?
- Oh, I have an interview in the morning.

27:24.059 --> 27:25.143
You do?

27:27.812 --> 27:29.898
- It's down to the last stage.
- [I-ra gasps]

27:30.440 --> 27:31.650
Are you serious?

27:31.733 --> 27:33.234
Nice! That's great!

27:33.318 --> 27:35.904
- Yeah, Won-jun!
- Congrats, man! [chuckles]

27:35.987 --> 27:39.157
Congratulations! Aw, that's my boy!

27:39.240 --> 27:41.409
Seriously, though, dang.
How are you still single?

27:41.493 --> 27:44.496
- What a waste this is. Am I right?
- You should've told us about it, huh?

27:45.080 --> 27:45.914
[Won-jun sighs]

27:47.666 --> 27:50.001
Ugh! This guy doesn't change!

27:50.085 --> 27:52.128
Why do you always keep stuff to yourself?

27:52.212 --> 27:55.256
- What else are you hiding?
- Let's see how the interview goes first.

27:55.340 --> 27:57.550
Knowing you,
you won't tell us till next year.

27:58.551 --> 27:59.928
I'll tell you either way, then.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.722
- [Yun-taek] Knock on wood.
- Knock on wood.

28:02.806 --> 28:05.016
- [Yun-taek] Don't jinx yourself!
- Knock on wood, everyone.

28:05.100 --> 28:07.894
- [Yun-taek] Congratulations!
- [all] Cheers!

28:07.977 --> 28:10.522
It's been ages
since we've had Jin-ju with us.

28:10.605 --> 28:14.150
Let's after-party at our house,
or else you're a traitor if you bail.

28:14.234 --> 28:16.695
- It's because of my interview.
- [Yun-taek] Come on. Get in.

28:16.778 --> 28:19.364
- Won-jun, you're not coming, right?
- Next time, I promise.

28:19.447 --> 28:21.199
[Yun-taek] Okay, bye.
Call us when you get it.

28:21.282 --> 28:24.577
- Call us even if you don't.
- Won-jun, you're gonna get that job.

28:24.661 --> 28:26.246
- [I-ra] Won-jun!
- [Won-jun] See you later.

28:26.329 --> 28:27.622
- [all] Bye.
- [Won-jun] Bye.

28:27.706 --> 28:28.540
[Jin-ju] Bye.

28:32.377 --> 28:33.294
[sighs]

28:35.755 --> 28:36.589
Hmm.

28:40.802 --> 28:41.636
[sighs]

29:44.365 --> 29:45.200
[sighs]

29:52.624 --> 29:53.833
[gate squeaks]

30:06.930 --> 30:08.932
[emotional music playing]

30:51.057 --> 30:51.933
Hello there.

30:56.813 --> 30:58.439
I thought you had gone.

31:00.024 --> 31:01.234
I left my jacket inside.

31:02.652 --> 31:04.821
Oh, um… you should go get it.

31:11.578 --> 31:13.580
[keypad beeping]

31:15.248 --> 31:16.416
[door beeps, opens]

31:18.167 --> 31:19.085
[door closes]

31:19.627 --> 31:20.545
[door beeps]

31:44.319 --> 31:46.321
[lounge music playing]

32:00.043 --> 32:02.754
- So, how is everyone?
- Good.

32:09.802 --> 32:10.970
They're all doing well.

32:14.265 --> 32:15.850
[Doona] Have you listened to my music?

32:36.120 --> 32:37.580
[Doona crying]

32:47.048 --> 32:49.050
[somber music playing]

33:26.921 --> 33:28.256
[pounding on door]

33:29.382 --> 33:30.383
[Doona] Lee Won-jun!

33:31.009 --> 33:33.052
- [pounding on door]
- [Doona] Hey!

33:35.930 --> 33:37.056
[pounding on door]

33:40.518 --> 33:44.439
"Take care of yourself"? That's all
you have to say to me after all this time?

33:44.522 --> 33:46.357
- Well, I'm sorry.
- [door opens]

33:48.234 --> 33:49.360
Let's talk inside.

34:06.794 --> 34:08.379
How are you so calm about this?

34:09.172 --> 34:10.298
Is that how it looks?

34:11.257 --> 34:12.842
Do you have any idea

34:14.052 --> 34:15.845
how much I needed you then?

34:16.763 --> 34:19.015
You're the only reason
I'm alive right now.

34:19.557 --> 34:20.600
Back then, I…

34:22.143 --> 34:24.270
I despised myself so much I couldn't even

34:25.021 --> 34:26.147
get up most days.

34:27.065 --> 34:30.401
I no longer worried about
what life had in store… until we met.

34:30.485 --> 34:32.278
Yeah, well, things are different now.

34:33.529 --> 34:35.073
You're right. It is different,

34:35.656 --> 34:37.158
'cause now I don't hate myself.

34:37.992 --> 34:39.494
I'm better than I've ever been.

34:39.577 --> 34:41.287
I'm no longer unstable or selfish.

34:41.370 --> 34:43.498
I'm sleeping well, and work's going great.

34:44.290 --> 34:46.626
And people stay by my side,
even without you.

34:48.628 --> 34:49.837
So now,

34:50.463 --> 34:52.006
I'll never need a man in my life again.

34:54.133 --> 34:55.134
I already know.

35:02.225 --> 35:04.352
So this time it's your turn to beg.

35:06.771 --> 35:07.730
Tell me you're sorry.

35:09.649 --> 35:11.025
And what you did was wrong.

35:16.072 --> 35:17.031
I'm sorry.

35:18.741 --> 35:20.159
I should've gone after you.

35:21.661 --> 35:22.870
Tell me you regret it.

35:24.288 --> 35:25.665
Say you regret it!

35:31.504 --> 35:32.630
I regret it.

35:35.341 --> 35:37.093
I should've fought for us. I was wrong.

35:39.011 --> 35:40.972
Now just leave me alone, okay?

35:43.599 --> 35:44.475
I'm begging you.

35:48.479 --> 35:49.772
I really missed you.

36:00.366 --> 36:01.826
I really missed you too.

36:04.287 --> 36:06.455
["Ordinary Day" playing]

36:22.305 --> 36:25.433
2027 NATIONAL CIVIL SERVANT LEVEL 5
OPEN COMPETITIVE RECRUITMENT EXAM

36:27.518 --> 36:29.854
LEE WON-JUN

37:45.388 --> 37:46.597
[inaudible]

37:46.681 --> 37:48.474
["Ordinary Day" continues]

38:21.882 --> 38:24.051
["Ordinary Day" continues]

38:27.888 --> 38:28.723
LEE DOONA

38:28.806 --> 38:29.765
YOU'RE AWESOME, DOONA

38:29.849 --> 38:31.559
[cheering]

39:13.434 --> 39:14.977
[music fades]

39:17.396 --> 39:18.314
[chuckles]

39:20.649 --> 39:24.111
[woman in Japanese] Here's your card, sir.
Here you go.

39:25.363 --> 39:26.447
Thank you.

39:27.907 --> 39:28.991
[man in English] Let's go.

39:29.658 --> 39:30.534
[Won-jun] Yes, sir.

39:36.457 --> 39:38.209
[in Japanese] It's Doona. Did you see her?

39:38.709 --> 39:39.752
So pretty!

39:42.129 --> 39:44.507
[in English] Oh, sir, it's this way.

39:45.758 --> 39:46.675
Please allow me.

39:53.557 --> 39:55.518
[emotional music playing]

39:55.601 --> 39:56.477
[sighs]
